  "text": "umably, we have a row of 16 chairs. We need to select 8 chairs such that no two selected chairs are next to each other. To solve this problem, let's first figure out the number of ways to select 8 chairs out of 16 such that no two selected chairs are adjacent.\n\n1. Start with the condition that no two selected chairs are adjacent. This means that we need to ensure there is at least one empty chair between any two selected chairs.\n\n2. For this, imagine we first select 8 chairs, leaving 8 empty chairs. We then need to ensure that no two selected chairs are adjacent. This can be modeled by selecting 8 chairs from the 17 possible positions (16 chairs + 1 empty chair between each selected chair).\n\n3. To do this, we can use the \"stars and bars\" method. We need to place 8 selected chairs and 8 empty chairs in a row of 16 chairs, ensuring that there is at least one empty chair between any two selected chairs. This can be visualized as placing 8 selected chairs and 8 empty chairs, with the requirement that no two selected chairs are adjacent.\n\n4. We can use the following formula: \\( \\binom{n}{k} \\), where \\( n \\) is the total number of positions (16 chairs + 1 empty chair between each selected chair), and \\( k \\) is the number of selected chairs (8).\n\n5. The formula to find the number of ways to select 8 chairs out of 16 such that no two selected chairs are adjacent is \\( \\binom{17}{8} \\).\n\n6. We need to compute \\( \\binom{17}{8} \\) and then find the remainder when this value is divided by 1000.\n\nLet's compute this step by step:\n\n\\[\n\\binom{17}{8} = \\frac{17!}{8!(17-8)!} = \\frac{17!}{8!9!}\n\\]\n\nWe will use Python to compute this value and then find the remainder when divided by 1000.\n```python\nimport math\n\n# Calculate the binomial coefficient\nn = 17\nk = 8\nbinom_coeff = math.comb(n, k)\n\n# Find the remainder when the binomial coefficient is divided by 1000\nremainder = binom_coeff % 1000\nprint((binom_coeff, remainder))\n```\n```output\n(24310, 310)\n```\nThe number of ways to select 8 chairs out of 16 such that no two selected chairs are adjacent is \\( \\binom{17}{8} = 24310 \\). The remainder when 24310 is divided by 1000 is \\( 310 \\).\n\nTherefore, the final answer is \\(\\boxed{310}\\).",
